# C1: Serial Communication

## 1. Communication architecture 

Node 1 (Serial Bridge for Arduino)- dedicated bridge between the arduino port and ROS. This publishes the sensor data to the sensor data topic 
                                    and subscribes to the led_controller topic from Node 2 to send commands to the Arduino.
Node 2 (User interface)- this node is dedicated to the user to handle the user input and interpreted the user command to Arduino through node 1 
led_controller - topic of Node 2
### Block diagram
```text
User input

   v

ROS2 Node 2 (reads the user input and publish the command to topic led_controller)

   v

ROS2 Node 1 (subscribes to led_controller, read and write serial port)

   v                            ^  (sensor data)

   v     (in the meantime Node 1 publishes the sensor values)

Serial communication

   v  (LED control commands)     ^  (sensor data)
 
Arduino[LED, Sensor]
```

QN: why two ROS2 nodes can be useful instead of putting everything into one node?
Ans: If we merge the nodes togather the nodes access to serial port will be in one pipe, means when we are taking user input, the incoming sensor data will freeze. 
Using 2 Nodes helps to continuously read, publish sersor data and take the user input. 
